  "question": {
    "text": "Let $a_n=\\left(1^2+2^2+\\ldots n^2\\right)^n$ and $b_n=n^n(n !)$. Then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FZf4V",
      "text": "$a_n < b_n \\forall n$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BvVB3",
      "text": "$a_n>b_n \\forall n$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "zDhmD",
      "text": "$a_n=b_n$ for infinitely many $n$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iBBsN",
      "text": "$a_n < b_n$ if $n$ be even and $a_n>b_n$ if $n$ be odd",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Using PMI $\\quad a_n>b_n \\quad\\left[{ }^* a_n>b_n \\forall n \\geq 2\\right.$ as $\\left.a_1=b_1\\right]$",
